DGREP(1)                       ZOAU Command Syntax                      DGREP(1)

NAME

	dgrep - Search for a pattern across all datasets (partitioned and
	sequential) matching one or more dataset patterns.

SYNOPSIS

	dgrep [-cdhijJnv] [-C <NUM>] <PATTERN> [<DATASET-PATTERN>]+

	-c
		Print only the number of matches for each dataset.

	-C <NUM>

		Display <NUM> lines of context around a match.

	-d
		Print out debug messages.

	-h
		Display syntax help.

	-i
		Ignore case.

	-j
		Print output in JSON format.

	-J
		Prints JSON output in a readable format.
		This option forces -j if it was not set.

	-n
		Display line numbers.

	-v
		Print names of datasets being searched

DESCRIPTION

	Search for <PATTERN> across the datasets specified in <DATASET-pattern>,
	writing matching lines to the console.

	If -i is specified, then the search will be case insensitive.

	If the -n option is specified, line numbers for the matching lines
	will be displayed.

	If context lines are requested with the -C option, then up to <NUM>
	lines before and after the matching line will also be printed.

DATASET PATTERNS

	The following rules apply to <DATASET-PATTERN>.

	The high-level qualifier (HLQ) must be specified in full.
	An asterisk (*) matches any sequence of characters.
	A question mark (?) matches a single character.

EXAMPLES

	Search for 'rexx' (case sensitive) in all datasets matching IBM.TSO.*:

		dgrep rexx 'IBM.TSO.*'

	Get a count of lines containing 'rexx' in all datasets matching IBM.TSO.*:

		dgrep -c rexx 'IBM.TSO.*'

	Search for 'Hi' (case insensitive) in all datasets matching IBM.*.C??:

		dgrep -i Hi 'IBM.*.C??'

	Search for 'test' in sequential and partitioned datasets,
	and display result in JSON format:

		dgrep -j test IBM.DATA.*

		Output with results found:

			{
				"data": {
					"IBM.DATA.SEQ": "test line\ntest line\ntest line",
					"IBM.DATA.PDS": {
						"MEMBER1": "test line\ntest line\ntest line",
						"MEMBER2": "test line\ntest line\ntest line",
						"MEMBER3": "test line\ntest line\ntest line"
					}
				},
				"program": "dgrep",
				"options": "-j",
				"rc": "0"
			}

		Output with no results found:

			{"data":{},"program":"dgrep","options":"-j","rc":"1"}

	Search for 'test' in the latest generation from the GDG IBM.GDG:

		dgrep test 'IBM.GDG(0)'

	Count records that contain 'test' in sequential and partitioned datasets,
	and display result in JSON format:

		dgrep -j -c test IBM.DATA.*

		Output with results found:

			{
				"data": {
					"IBM.TEST.SEQ": "4",
					"IBM.TEST.PDS": {
						"MEMBER1": "4",
						"MEMBER2": "4",
						"MEMBER3": "20"
					}
				},
				"program": "dgrep",
				"options": "-j",
				"rc": "0"
			}

		Output with no results found:

			{"data":{"IBM.TEST.SEQ":"0","IBM.TEST.PDS":"0"},"program":"dgrep","options":"-j -c","rc":"0"}

EXIT VALUES

	0
		At least one match for the pattern was found.

  	1
		No matches for the pattern were found.

  	2
		An error occurred trying to list dataset. See error messages for details.

  	4
		Incorrect options specified.

  	other
		Error in search. See error messages for details.

SEE ALSO

	grep(1)
